# Harikane et al. (2025), "JWST, ALMA, and Keck Spectroscopic Constraints on the UV Luminosity Functions at
#   z~7-14: Clumpiness and Compactness of the Brightest Galaxies in the Early Universe", ApJ 980, 138 (2025),
#   doi:10.3847/1538-4357/ad9b2c
# arXiv:2406.18352v2 (accepted version), Table 2 ("Spectroscopic Constraints on the Luminosity Function")
# SPECTROSCOPY-ONLY number densities (only spectroscopically confirmed galaxies are counted)
# x: M_UV (AB; wavelength not stated in paper, compiled from literature photometry) -> M1600 in info.txt,
#    as for the existing Harikane2022/Harikane2023 entries
# Phi: linear, Mpc^-3 mag^-1 (written exactly as tabulated, in e-notation); asymmetric 1-sigma errors
#      (Poisson [Gehrels86] + cosmic variance)
# Cosmology: Planck18 (h = 0.6766, Om = 0.3111)
# Rows marked (dagger) in the paper are taken from Harikane et al. 2024, ApJ 960, 56 (arXiv:2304.06658).
# LOWER LIMITS in Table 2 cannot be represented by the loader and are EXCLUDED from the data columns;
#   they are listed as comments below. Upper limits are in Harikane2025_ulimit/.
# Redshift bin: z_spec = 13.5-15.0 (z~14); GS-z14-0 with the Robertson+2024 (JOF) survey volume
# Excluded lower limit: M=-19.0 >3.7e-5
# M_UV   phi   sigma_upper   sigma_lower
-20.8  3.7e-5  8.7e-5  3.6e-5
